The original files in macos/Sources/UsageCore/Upstream and selected ClaudeSubscriptionTests,
now archived on the legacy branch under rust-validation/,
derive from AIUsage. Modifications include removing proxy/server and OAuth refresh
code, adding memory-only read-only quota fetches, isolating storage paths, extracting
shared data types, and extending the streaming JSON projection for Codex usage.
The QuotaBar projection skips unused conversation and tool metadata while preserving
numeric usage fields, and daily aggregation avoids per-event string formatting.
New application UI, scheduling, keychain integration, and local usage aggregation
are provided as part of this independent lightweight adaptation.
The activity cards in macos/Sources/QuotaBar/ActivityView.swift adapt the upstream
DashboardView+Heatmap.swift layout, calendar grid, and tooltip presentation.
Colors and provider symbols use QuotaBar's shared application theme.
CodexLogo.png, ClaudeLogo.svg, and GeminiLogo.png are the unmodified provider
logos from the upstream assets.
The data adapter uses QuotaBar's bounded local token reports without proxy ledgers.
Codex browser sign-in now delegates to the locally installed official Codex CLI
in an isolated temporary home. App-owned OAuth refresh and rotation persistence
are implemented separately, using the public Codex client parameters also present
in the upstream Codex provider. Imported CLI files remain read-only.

No CLIProxyAPI, Sparkle, browser runtime, or upstream sponsor assets are bundled.

Windows provider parsing, subscription status line preservation and local usage
aggregation in windows/src/QuotaBar.Core and windows/src/QuotaBar.Windows port the
corresponding QuotaBar/AIUsage rules. Windows DPAPI/ACL storage, native tray and WPF
processes are new platform implementations. Shared synthetic fixtures exercise
both native implementations. shared/assets retains the existing logo originals.
The archived Windows implementation includes Microsoft's .NET runtime with its
license and notices. Current Rust packages include no managed runtime. Their
three version-only compatibility DLLs contain no methods or entry points.
The Windows menu scroll arrows in windows/assets/MenuScrollArrows.png are
the ScrollButtonUp and ScrollButtonDown images from .NET Windows Forms.
Copyright (c) .NET Foundation and Contributors. They are distributed under the
MIT license included in licenses/Windows Forms/LICENSE in the Windows distribution.
The Rust dashboard uses AccessKit. The vendored accesskit_consumer 0.31.0 is
copyright 2021 The AccessKit Authors and distributed under Apache License 2.0.
QuotaBar enables writable scrollbars in its accessibility state mapping.
The vendored AccessKit Windows adapter 0.29.2 exposes expandable controls to
UI Automation. Its licenses and Chromium notice are in licenses/AccessKit/.
The native Rust Claude callback adapts the same AIUsage subscription snapshot,
profile and command forwarding rules for the original Windows and macOS formats.
The Rust macOS connection also adapts AIUsage's subscription installation,
reconnection, command backup and field-level restoration rules.
The Rust usage scanner ports the existing streaming projection, session fork
accounting and Claude message aggregation for both platforms.
The Rust quota adapters and status summaries preserve QuotaBar's platform-specific
display rules. The Windows notification icon uses GDI+ and the shared AppMark.
The Rust credential parser and OAuth rotation retain QuotaBar and AIUsage's
workspace identity rules and the existing platform-specific import formats.
The Windows native provider transport uses libcurl and Schannel for explicitly
configured proxies. The libcurl, curl-rust, schannel and zlib notices are
included in licenses/libcurl/LICENSE in the Windows distribution.

Current Rust implementations in native/claude, native/codex_sessions, native/usage,
native/provider_requests and native/ui/activity.rs preserve the corresponding
AIUsage-derived rules and attribution above. Swift and C# application/test sources
are maintained only on the legacy branch. AppIcon-4.icns and AppDockIcon.png are
pre-rendered from the same QuotaBar AppMark.svg used by the validated native build.
